{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/11236","id":5355421724,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABPzVAHA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11236","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11236.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11236.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11236","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/11236/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/11236/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11236/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/ff84e486c45bfdb1f4ca9a79b7ad11e131a037b5","number":11236,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(mcpx): wire identity failover into the daemon call path (#8017)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements piece 1 of #8017 (daemon call-path wiring; follow-on to #7948, queue task 20062):\n\n- `mcpauth/toolresult.go` (new): translates an error `tools/call` result — or a call error's text — into an `*mcpauth.APIError` Classify can read (status extraction, soft markers, Retry-After). Successful results never translate, however rate-limit-shaped their content.\n- `pool/failover.go` (new): `Pool.Call` runs failover-configured servers through `Rotator.Do`. A soft block rotates the identity, the instance serving the key is respawned on the rotated credential (`ReleaseKey`; the fresh spawn's `resolveAuth` reads the persisted rotation state), and the call is retried — the calling session never sees the soft block. Hard blocks and all non-block outcomes settle byte-for-byte as before (sentinel the rotator treats as hard). `resolveAuth` and `Call` share one construction site (`failoverRotator`); rotations log through the pool lifecycle log naming both identities.\n- `pool.go`: existing `Call` body becomes `callOnce`; unused `net/http` import dropped.\n- `testsupport/fakemcp`: script responses gain `isError` results and an `ifEnv`/`else` conditional, so a fake's answer can depend on the credential it was spawned with.\n- `doc/fleet/mcp.md`: failover paragraph now describes the call path.\n\nOracle tests (all pass on the laptop, post-rebase):\n- mcpauth translation: secondary-limit 403 rotates; 429 + Retry-After rotates; marker-less 403 is hard; a successful result about rate limits never translates; unrelated errors never translate.\n- pool end-to-end (`TestFailoverCallSoftBlockRotatesRespawnsAndRetries`): fake spawned with identity \"first\" soft-blocks; the caller sees only `served-by-second` and the persisted rotation state names \"second\". `TestFailoverCallHardBlockSurfacesUnchanged`: hard block returns unchanged, no rotation.\n- `go build ./...`, `go vet`, mcpauth + fakemcp suites pass. Full pool suite: one flaky failure in `TestDefaultConfigStdioRunsSupervised` (supervised-child reap timing under suite load) — passes standalone in this worktree and on clean main; unrelated to this change.\n\nNot in this PR — piece 2 (live activation) is split to a follow-on queue task with the evidence: the github server is absent from both the live `~/.config/mcpx/config.json` and the repo `.mcpx.json`, and no source checked (issue #8017, doc/fleet/mcp.md, #7948) names the three GitHub App identities / App IDs / installation IDs / secret-store names to enroll, so there is nothing well-defined to activate yet.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797504669&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11236&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11236&signature=bfdf9b883959e81f86ed255d13650d0fc93ad403a559d507a43b1ed030ae00a0\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/11236?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"creat